 },
 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:09:06.212973Z",
 "text": "Under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, parties to a tenancy may mutually agree to terminate it, and where such an agreement is reached, no formal notice of termination is required from either party (subsection 37(2)). Because the clause specifies that this agreement occurs *after* the tenancy has begun (avoiding the statutory prohibition against requiring an agreement to terminate as a condition of entering into a tenancy), it is fully consistent with the Act and enforceable.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 37",
